    "title": "Advanced Linking Words I",
    "title_ko": "고급 접속 부사 (nevertheless/furthermore/consequently)",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Formal connecting adverbs organize ideas in writing and formal speech: 'nevertheless' (contrast, despite this), 'furthermore' (adding a point), 'consequently' (result). They usually start a new sentence and are followed by a comma.",
    "explanation_ko": "격식체 접속 부사는 글쓰기·격식적 발화에서 생각을 정리합니다: 'nevertheless'(대조, 그럼에도), 'furthermore'(추가), 'consequently'(결과). 보통 새 문장을 시작하며 뒤에 콤마가 옵니다.",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "The plan was risky. Nevertheless, we proceeded.",
        "ko": "계획은 위험했어요. 그럼에도 우리는 진행했어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "Sales increased. Furthermore, customer satisfaction improved.",
        "ko": "매출이 늘었어요. 게다가 고객 만족도도 향상됐어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "The flight was delayed. Consequently, we missed our connection.",
        "ko": "비행이 지연됐어요. 그 결과 환승편을 놓쳤어요."
      }
    ]
  },
